Z||000000||PAUL88GT||05-18-2001||12:25 PM||||I just installed a new subwoofer speaker in my 86SE.<P>The new speaker came from Radio Shack (part number 40-1032, 5.25 inch woofer).  Price was $20 plus tax.  I am not sure how it sounds since I have the interior completely removed for my restoration.  I will update the post when I get the interior put back together. I also need to get a new radio.<P>I did have to modify the factory speaker cover at each corner to make it fit into the speaker frame.  I used a dremel tool to cut away some of the plastic around the bolt holes.  It looks no different than factory once installed into the enclosure.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierojunky||05-18-2001||01:21 PM||||RadioShack speakers - you get what you paid for - I replaced the front speakers in my car with RadioShacks and they are junk now - hey i got a year out of them.  ||||reg||10
